A||||19||Scott||ADS Superchip B (strip) installed...||||14||
Z||000000||Scott||08-10-2001||06:50 PM||||and it's very cool.  Both my copilot (wife) and I agree it was a great addition to the car.  The SOTP (seat-of-the-pants) HP meter feels like about a 10% increase in HP.  Just thought I'd drop a line to say that this chip IS worth getting if anyone is interested.<BR>Scott||||reg||14
Z||000001||Shaun41178||08-10-2001||11:02 PM||||HAHAHAHAAHa you crack me up<P>10% so like a 14 hp increase?  WOW!!<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||08-11-2001||12:07 AM||||Yeah before I change my opinion on chips, I want to see Dyno proof.  Until then, I maintain they will provide no performance increase (but can be good for dealing with fuel issues or eliminating EGR)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Scott||08-11-2001||03:24 AM||||Shaun- Why the cynicism?  I'm just trying to pass on some info to those that may be interested.  In my opinion, a 14 HP increase is significant, considering the motor produces so little HP from the factory.  (I got the chip cheap and the mods were easy, so I consider it worth while.) <BR>Black- I put the chip in a spare ECM I have, so I can easily do a dyno test w/ factory vs. ADS when I get access to a dyno.  I haven't removed the EGR yet, but it'll be gone by Sun.  (Putting in the chip, lower temp. thermostat,  and straight pipe was enough for one afternoon.)<p>[This message has been edited by Scott (edited 08-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Shaun41178||08-11-2001||12:27 PM||||the cynicism is from the fact that I have seen actual dyno results of these "performance chips" and the most they gave over a stock chip was 1-2 peak hp and they lost hp in other areas of the rpm band.  So I know for a fact that they don't do diddly squat.  Yet you people come on here saying you can tell a difference with a performance chip when there is very little if any at all.  You are the same people that say they got 15 hp from a Spiralmax.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Take your chip out without telling your wife and then go for some nice full throttle stomps and then say to her "Man I can't believe how much power this new chip has given me."  If she trully feels the difference from the stock to the performance one then she should be able to tell that you secretly went back to the stock one and she might say something like, "Actually honey it doesn't feel as fast as the other day."  if she says "I know it is much faster"(oops not good thing to say) when the stock chip was in it, then she never felt anything in the first place.<P>I can guarantee you that you will not pick up 14 hp from just the chip swap.  Since you have an extra computer and can swap in 5 minutes you can get 2 dyno runs in pretty quickly without weather conditions changing drastically.  Are both computers you have from the same year and tranny fiero so the test results can be similar?<P>How about we make a bet.  If you get 14 hp from just the chip change and chip change alone, I will pay for your dyno time(up to $60)  a +13 hp increase will not be enough as it has to be 14 or more.  And if it doesn't make at least 14 hp more then you have to respond from now on to all the "Performance Chip" posts and be cynical to the people saying they got big gains and you also have to post your dyno results to the forum in each of these posts too using PIP.  Trust me it will get old after abut 2-3 times and you will get tired of doing it.<P>Anyone on this forum living near Scott and would like to witness this event as an impartial observer would be great.  Pics of your car on the dyno would be great for proof that you went or even a video of your car spinning up the rollers would be better.  Sorry but I don't completely trust you with me being here in florida and you being in WI and the fact that it is over $60.  I hope you can be honest about it.  Do you accept the Challenge?????<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||08-11-2001||01:05 PM||||I suspect that any performance gains you felt came from the low temp thermostat and straight pipe.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mickey_Moose||08-11-2001||01:24 PM||||actually there is a easy way of doing this...take both chips out have someone mix them up and put one in - you don't know which - take a drive, change chips (do it a couple of times to make sure) - see which one is better without your knowledge of which one is in.<P>Tim<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||08-11-2001||01:36 PM||||Well, removing the cat WILL get you about 5HP and make the car rev freer.  That has been documented on a dyno.  Now that you have the car setup for the chip (thermo, pipe, etc) I'd love to see a back to back comparison!  If the chip gives you more than a couple HP without loosing much, if any, at lower rpms, I'm gonna get one.  I just want to make sure I find one that actually works.  That, and that'll save me from having to get a new EGR tube!  The chip can't be much more than just repairing my EGR. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Capt Fiero||08-11-2001||02:20 PM||||The HP gains are not a concern in my case, the reason that I feel a chip is a good thing, is that it kils the EGR system electronicly. 2nd it gets rid of the rev limiter on pre 88 fiero's.  It gets rid of the injector shut off on deceleration.  I am not sure what it does to timming, I am told that it advances your total timming, so people that have already advanced there timming may actully loose power due to detonation unless they first retard it back to stock.  Chips are designed to enhance a factory stock motor and hence if you have made any adjustments to your engine or emmisions the effects can be severly good or bad.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Dave Gunsul||08-11-2001||10:52 PM||||I've said it many times before and i'll say it again: my ADS Strip Chip does make a difference in my car. However, there's<BR>no way it made 14 HP!<P>Since others on here chose to go out of their way to be unfairly rude to others on this subject then so will I: The know-it-alls<BR>who claim to have tested these chips could not have tested all of the chips out there and should really refrain from flaming since their data is obviously incomplete as well!!<BR>If you don't agree with someone that's fine but to go out of your way to be rude and talk down to someone is really uncalled for.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000010||Scott||08-12-2001||12:02 PM||||OK guys here's the full deal...  It's a '85 GT 4spd.  I put in a 180* thermostat and Rodney's 195* (?) fan switch 4 weeks ago.  I went from a glass pack (put on before I owned the car) to a straight pipe last weekend.  The straight pipe doesn't feel like much of a change from the glass pack with or without the ADS chip so I may go back to it.  (I like the glass pack + muffler sound better). I put the chip in on Tues, and put in a 160* thermo on Weds.  I haven't checked the timing because it runs v. good, but if you'd like I will.  I won't be pulling the EGR or TB coolant lines this weekend, but I may get to it in the week.  <BR>  I have no idea how much extra HP the chip provides, it may be only 1%.  I was guessing at 10%.  Maybe it just increases the timing, I'll check it eventually.  My point was, there IS a noticeable difference.  Putting in the chip made the biggest difference, so I thought it was worth mentioning. <BR>  The nearest dyno I know of is 2 hrs. away.  I will eventually check it out there, but it's not high on my list of priorities.  I understand the skepticism and I wish I could give any doubters a ride.  As I said before, I got the chip relatively cheap, so I think it was worth it.  In hind sight, I would install it again, but I don't think I'd write about it again :~)<BR>Scott<p>[This message has been edited by Scott (edited 08-12-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000011||rmcmsw||08-12-2001||09:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Capt Fiero:<BR><B>The HP gains are not a concern in my case, the reason that I feel a chip is a good thing, is that it kils the EGR system electronicly. 2nd it gets rid of the rev limiter on pre 88 fiero's.  It gets rid of the injector shut off on deceleration.  I am not sure what it does to timming, I am told that it advances your total timming, so people that have already advanced there timming may actully loose power due to detonation unless they first retard it back to stock.  Chips are designed to enhance a factory stock motor and hence if you have made any adjustments to your engine or emmisions the effects can be severly good or bad.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Shaun41178||08-13-2001||01:24 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR> The know-it-alls<BR>who claim to have tested these chips could not have tested all of the chips out there and should really refrain from flaming since their data is obviously incomplete as well!!<P><BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks for calling me a know it all.  Don't worry I won't let it go to my head.  <P>Not tested all of these chips you ask Dave?<BR> Lets see how many are there in mass production that most/all Fiero owners get?  Hmmmm I am thinking hard now.  Oh thats right!!!  A whole whopping two.  Hypertech and ADS.  And which ones did I see dyno tests for on a Fiero?  Yes thats right!!  Both the Hypertech and the ADS ones.  And both were the "off-road" chip which is supposed to be the more "performance" one.  Both chips did give hp increase over the stock one.  Go back and read Dave I never said that it didn't and I never said that it didn't with your car.  However I did say that it was 2 peak hp in the extreme upper rpm(over 5500) and lost some low end torque.  <P>Go get yours dyno tested Dave and your results will be the same.  I guarantee it to be with a 1-3 peak increase in hp.  Do I think that increase in hp given by the chip versus the cost of it and having to constantly run premium fuel at more cost worth the money??  I say in no way it is.  But if you want to go pay $100+ for a chip and then the extra cost to run premium fuel every week then be my guest.  I have the facts and I try to prove to you guys but not many listen.  Too many @ss-o-meter guys on this forum.  I guarantee you can't feel less then 5 hp and that is what the chip is making at most.  How do I know you can't feel it?  Cause a gain of 5 hp is like a difference of .05 sec in the qtr mile.  Are you going to tell a difference from a 15.00 run compared to a 15.05 run?  Hell no you are not.  I don't care how accurate you think your butt is.<P>You want to know the difference between the stock chip and the performance chips?  The timing.  Thats it.  Its advances the timing a few degrees more then the stock chip does.  How do I know this?  I have had conversations with people that have diseccted the chips programing and compared it to a stock one.  Save money and just advance your distributor 2-4 degrees over the base 10 degree mark and it will be the same as adding a chip but a lot less money.<P>You like data?  Well what do you think about that data?<P><P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds||||reg||4
Z||000013||terryk||08-13-2001||01:39 AM||||Geez, is this worth it? <P>Send me the chip, I'll tell you exactly what was changed. ||||reg||5
Z||000014||DRH||08-13-2001||10:07 AM||||I suspect you guys are comparing apples and oranges. Aren't dyno runs done at WOT? Most of <B>my</B> ass-o-meter runs are a combination of spirited (but not WOT) takeoffs with a couple of WOT runs mixed in.<P>The chip was originally design to balance power, emissions and fuel economy. I suspect power was weighted more heavily at WOT and the other two more heavily under other conditions. If someone designs a chip without worrying about emissions or fuel economy it seems they could "find" some power. It also makes sense that the improvement would be minimal at WOT but could be more significant (even enough to feel) under other conditions.<P>It would be interesting to see terryk's analysis of where they "tweaked" it...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Slammed Fiero||08-13-2001||10:58 AM||||I dunno shaun , my ass is pretty sensitive.<P>I have never tired a chip , I have been on Fiero lists and whatnot for the last 6 years. MY impression after hearing what people say about chips , is that a Dorito gives about the Same HP as a chip.<P>Also people will feel what they want to believe. If I spent the cash on a chip , I'm sure I would have hi hopes for it too. Fact is , nothing happens. Shaun failed to mention his custom burned prom , that was setup for his NOS , it made no difference either I believe.<P>Chips make a difference on Turbo cars , Rx7's can get 60hp from a computer , Our 911 saw 17 rear wheel hp with a Motec Stage 3 brain kit.<P>GM did a good job designing the chip in a fiero. Some people have a hard time hearing they wasted money.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Leadfoot||08-13-2001||11:26 AM||||Anyone know where I can get my ass-o-meter calibrated, I think it's off.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Seriously, though, I was one of those people who bought a hypertech chip and to be honest I can't tell the difference from stock.  I really wish I put that $100 bucks somewhere else...like new rear tires, or rear sway bar.  Just my 0.02 guys.||||reg||1
Z||000017||terryk||08-13-2001||12:17 PM||||Actually, I was wondering if the bulging veins and throbbing temples is worth it.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Dave Gunsul||08-13-2001||01:37 PM||||Shaun: Before you and I get really yelling at each other i'd like to say that normally<BR>when I read your posts you are level headed and informative! Normally you write things that I agree with and if I don't I have always felt that I could give my point of view and we could have a grown up discussion.<BR>This time however you came out and basically laughed in someones face!!! I don't agree with Scott's claim of 14 HP either but I certainly didn't feel that he deserved such and out and out HOSTILE reply that you gave him. He was more than likely exaggerating anyway.<P>Secondly: There are more chips than two.<BR>Jet, Associated Auto (Fiero only business),<BR>and one other company that escapes me right now make chips for the Fiero. Superchips will<BR>also make a custom chip for the Fiero or anything else for that matter.<P>Third: Chips make a much larger difference on auto cars than they do on stick shift cars. I'm sure that you're going to tell me to just shift the auto manually but it's still a difference none the less.<BR>As stated earlier: the chip also makes it possible to dump the emission equip. which will also improve power.<P>Lastly: I think if you reread what you originally wrote you might see why someone might take offense at it. Others in this thread have disagreed but you'll notice that they didn't do it in the same way. Read Leadfoots response for instance.<P>Sorry for the length. Hopefully there won't be any lasting bad feelings between us.<BR>There isn't on this end anyway.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||4
